Export data to CSV format using PapaParse library.

Converts an array of objects to CSV format and triggers a browser download.
Each object's keys become column headers (unless custom headers are provided).

@param data - Array of objects to export (each object is a row)
@param filename - Output filename (should include .csv extension)
@param headers - Optional array of column names to include (filters/orders columns)
@returns void - Triggers browser download

@example
```typescript
// Export all fields
exportToCSV(participants, 'participants-export.csv');

// Export specific columns in order
exportToCSV(participants, 'participants.csv', ['name', 'email', 'role']);
```

