Singleton service for handling and tracking session errors.

Classifies errors by type, generates recovery suggestions, maintains
an error log, and can attempt automatic recovery for certain error types.

@example
```typescript
const handler = SessionErrorHandler.getInstance();

try {
  // session operation
} catch (error) {
  const sessionError = handler.handleError(error, 'serialization');
  console.log(handler.formatUserFriendlyMessage(sessionError));
}
```

