Singleton service for session state persistence to localStorage.

Handles serialization of complex session objects (with Maps, Dates, circular refs)
into JSON-safe format, auto-saves at intervals, and provides recovery on reload.

@example
```typescript
const persistence = SessionPersistenceService.getInstance();

// Register for auto-save
persistence.registerSessionForAutoSave(sessionId, session);

// Manual save
await persistence.saveSession(session, `session:${session.id}`);

// Load persisted session
const session = await persistence.loadSession(key, availablePlugins);
```

Singleton service for monitoring storage quota and preventing overflow.

Automatically monitors storage usage and performs cleanup when thresholds
are exceeded. Supports both web browsers (using StorageManager API) and
desktop Electron environments.

@example
```typescript
const monitor = StorageQuotaMonitor.getInstance();

// Configure thresholds
monitor.setWarningThreshold(0.70);   // Warn at 70%
monitor.setEmergencyThreshold(0.85); // Emergency cleanup at 85%

// Get current quota info
const quota = await monitor.getQuotaInfo();
console.log(`Using ${quota.percentage * 100}% of storage`);
```

