Server-Sent Events (SSE) client for unidirectional event streaming.

Lighter-weight alternative to WebSocket for receive-only scenarios.
Ideal for session event streams where client doesn't need to send data.

@example
```typescript
const sseClient = new SSEClient('/sessions/sess-123/events');

sseClient.on('session:update', (data) => {
  console.log('Session updated:', data);
});

sseClient.connect();

// Later, clean up
sseClient.disconnect();
```

